      "text": "Guanajuato – Guadalajara"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "0e5bc689dd7c8b7f24b47a106f76eefba1c6d8f294317622c064cac39998df4c",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-mwa5muwazo597oeipo",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, travel to Guadalajara.\n\nThe tour introduces you to the city’s main sights, including the cathedral, which features neoclassical architectural elements, and the Plaza de Armas in front of it.\n\nThen visit Hospicio Cabañas, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The neoclassical building houses artworks and murals by Mexican artist José Clemente Orozco.\n\nAnother stop is San Juan de Dios Market, where you can get a glimpse of everyday life in the city and browse a wide range of goods, handicrafts and local food.\n\nAfter the tour, check in and stay overnight in Guadalajara."
    },
